  "description": "PostgreSQL for .NET apps on Entity Framework Core: `UseRaskPostgres(...)` is a drop-in replacement for `UseNpgsql` that applies the production session settings (`statement_timeout`, `lock_timeout`, `idle_in_transaction_session_timeout`) to every connection the context opens and turns on Npgsql's transient-failure retrying. SQLite stays Rask's default; this is the door out when one box is no longer enough.",
